      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not clear to me that libusb_get_string_descriptor() is guaranteed to return a NULL-terminated string[1].  If for example strlen(serial) \u003e sizeof(sn), then in theory this could result in a false positive match.\n\nI think the safest option is to use the size returned by libusb_get_string_descriptor_ascii().\n\nsn_size \u003d libusb_get_string_descriptor_ascii(...);\nif (... || (serial \u0026\u0026 (!sn_size || retval !\u003d strlen(sn) || memcmp(sn, serial, retval)))) {\n  ...\n}\n\n\n[1] http://libusb.sourceforge.net/api-1.0/group__desc.html",
